.Dd July 26, 2026
.Dt GITM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gitm
.Nd multi-repo Git registry manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hrv
.Op Fl L Ar level
.Op Fl F Ar file
.Ar command
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a fast command-line utility for inspecting and managing multiple Git
repositories using the Git CLI.
It maintains a registry of local repositories and provides commands to list,
filter, search, and operate on them in parallel.
.Pp
Repositories are identified by a unique name and can be annotated with tags
and groups for filtering.
.Nm
requires no third-party dependencies beyond a C17 compiler and pthreads.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Show help message and exit.
.It Fl v , -version
Show version and exit.
.It Fl L , Fl -log-level Ns = Ns Ar level
Set log verbosity.
Valid values:
.Dq off ,
.Dq fatal ,
.Dq error ,
.Dq warn ,
.Dq info ,
.Dq debug ,
.Dq trace .
.It Fl F , Fl -log-file Ns = Ns Ar file
Write log output to
.Ar file
instead of stderr.
.It Fl E , Fl -edit-entry
Open
.Pa registered_repos.txt
in
.Ev $EDITOR .
.It Fl S , Fl -shell-completion Ns = Ns Ar shell
Output shell completion script.
Supported shells:
.Dq bash ,
.Dq zsh ,
.Dq fish .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss list (ls)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm list [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
List registered repositories.
Each entry shows its name, path, tags, and groups.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss add
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm add Ar path Op Ar name Op Fl t Ar tags Op Fl g Ar groups
.Ed
.Pp
Register a Git repository.
.Ar path
must be an absolute path to a Git working tree.
If
.Ar name
is omitted, it is derived from the last path component.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tags
Comma-separated tags (e.g.
.Dq work,c ) .
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar groups
Comma-separated groups (e.g.
.Dq projects ) .
.El
.Ss remove (rm)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm remove Ar name
.Ed
.Pp
Unregister a repository by name.
The on-disk repository is not deleted.
.Ss rename
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm rename Ar old-name Ar new-name
.Ed
.Pp
Rename a registered repository alias.
.Ss clone
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm clone Ar url Op Ar name
.Ed
.Pp
Clone a repository from
.Ar url
into the current directory and register it.
If
.Ar name
is omitted, it is derived from the URL.
.Ss status (st, s)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm status [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show the status of all registered repositories, including current branch,
working tree cleanliness, and commit counts.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss info (i)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm info Ar name
.Ed
.Pp
Show detailed repository metadata including path, tags, groups, branch,
remote URL, and last commit information.
.Ss exec (x)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm exec Ar name Ar command ...
.Ed
.Pp
Run an arbitrary Git command on a registered repository.
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm exec myrepo log --oneline -5
.Ed
.Ss open (o)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm open Ar name
.Ed
.Pp
Open a repository in
.Ev $EDITOR .
If
.Ev $EDITOR
is not set, falls back to
.Ev $VISUAL .
.Ss doctor (doc, d)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm doctor [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Health check all registered repositories.
Verifies each repository exists on disk and is a valid Git working tree.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss recent (r)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm recent [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
List repositories sorted by last commit date (most recent first).
In non-table mode, shows relative timestamps (e.g.
.Dq 3 hours ago ) .
In table mode, includes both relative and absolute commit dates.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss summary (sum)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm summary [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ]
.Ed
.Pp
Show aggregate statistics: total repositories, total branches, and combined
disk usage.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.El
.Ss search (find, f)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm search Op Ar pattern
.Ed
.Pp
Search registered repositories by name or path.
If no pattern is given, lists all repositories.
.Ss list-tag (tags, lt)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm list-tag [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show tags across all registered repositories with their messages.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss remote (rem)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm remote [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show remote URL settings for each registered repository.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss last (log, l)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm last [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show the last commit log entry for each registered repository.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss branch (br, b)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm branch [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show local branches for each registered repository.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss clean (prune)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm clean [-n]
.Ed
.Pp
Remove repositories from the registry that no longer exist on disk.
By default, orphans are removed; use
.Fl n
to preview without making changes.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Show orphans without removing them.
.El
.Ss stale (old)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm stale [-d Ar days ] [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show repositories with no commits in the last
.Ar days
days (default: 30).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl -days Ns = Ns Ar N
Staleness threshold in days.
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss stash (st)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm stash [-t Ar tag ] [-g Ar group ] [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Run
.Ic git stash
across repositories with dirty working trees.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl -tag Ns = Ns Ar tag
Filter by tag.
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Filter by group.
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Ss stats (ts)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm stats [-T]
.Ed
.Pp
Show tag and group frequency summary across all registered repositories.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl T , Fl -table
Show output in tabular format.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
stores its registry in a plain-text file.
Each line has the format:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/path/to/repo:name[:tags[:groups]]
.Ed
.Pp
Tags and groups are comma-separated.
A maximum of 50 repositories is supported.
.Pp
The config file is located at (in order of priority):
.Bl -enum -width "1."
.It
.Ev $XDG_DATA_HOME Ns / Ns Pa gitm/registered_repos.txt
.It
on macOS:
.Ev $HOME Ns / Ns Pa Library/Application Support/gitm/registered_repos.txt
.It
on Linux:
.Ev $HOME Ns / Ns Pa .local/share/gitm/registered_repos.txt
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev GITM_THREADS
Maximum number of threads for parallel operations.
Defaults to the number of CPU cores, capped at 8.
.It Ev EDITOR
Editor used by
.Ic gitm open
and
.Ic gitm --edit-entry .
.It Ev VISUAL
Fallback editor if
.Ev EDITOR
is not set.
.It Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the config file (defaults to
.Pa ~/.local/share ) .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME Ns / Ns Pa gitm/registered_repos.txt
Repository registry (see
.Sx CONFIGURATION ) .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Register a repository:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm add ~/src/myproject myproj -t work,c
.Ed
.Pp
List all registered repos in a table:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm list -T
.Ed
.Pp
Show repos not committed to in 60+ days:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm stale -d 60
.Ed
.Pp
Run a git command across a repo:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm exec myproj log --oneline -3
.Ed
.Pp
Clean up orphaned entries:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm clean -n   # preview
gitm clean      # remove
.Ed
.Pp
Clone and register in one step:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gitm clone https://github.com/user/repo
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1
